! name: Daily Driver
! description: Light-touch general search. Downranks SEO/content-farm domains and low-value aggregator/scraper sites, without hiding anything outright. Meant to be used for everyday search, not a narrow topic Goggle.
! public: false
! author: Mark

! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Philosophy: this is NOT a $discard-everything-then-boost Goggle. The goal
! is to nudge the default Brave ranking away from known SEO spam and
! content-farm domains, while leaving recall wide open for everything else.
! Strengths are kept low (1-2) so this stays "light touch" rather than a
! full block-list.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

! --- SEO / content-farm / listicle mills ---------------------------------
! TODO: fill in with domains you personally keep bouncing off of. Starting
! placeholders below — replace/expand as you notice patterns while browsing.
$downrank=2,site=pinterest.com
$downrank=2,site=quora.com
$downrank=1,site=answers.com

! --- Low-effort "SEO-optimized" tutorial/listicle aggregators ------------
! These often reword/scrape better sources for search ranking purposes.
$downrank=2,site=geeksforgeeks.org
$downrank=1,site=w3schools.com

! --- Copycat / scraped Stack Overflow & GitHub mirrors -------------------
! See tech-research.goggle for a more thorough version of this list; a
! couple of the worst offenders are downranked here too since they pollute
! general search, not just technical search.
$downrank=3,site=itectec.com
$downrank=3,site=qastack.com

! --- Add more entries below as you identify them -------------------------
